it's America recycles week and across  the country recycling continues to run  into roadblocks but when a community has  great access to recycling like ours it's  hard to find good reasons not to recycle  Republic Services and our local  governments have been improving access  to recycling they've put single blue  cards in our Valley neighborhoods and  coordinating with garbage pickup days  getting recycling into apartments and  more businesses I spoke to Keith  Harrison she's the CEO of the recycling  partnership a non-profit dedicated to  improving recycling practices about how  we can do more  so when we look at Las Vegas we see  about 90 access rate we see really high  access rate compared to the rest of the  country that means that people have a  good opportunity either at their  apartment or at their home to be able to  recycle now then the second part comes  in on are they sure what to put in the  bin uh this recycling landscape is  always changing things that didn't used  to be recyclable are becoming recyclable  because because Community make leaders  and companies and non-profits like ours  are leaning in hard to make more things  recyclable so we need the public to stay  on their toes and keep in touch with  that so that means education will be an  ongoing exercise to know what's  recyclable and then the last piece is  does it turn into something new so we  put it all into one big bin it goes to a  Murph a material recovery facility to  get separated out so that newspaper is  in one place and cans are in another  only at that point are we able to turn  those things into their next life  well Harrison says we all have to  cooperate to make recycling work  effectively the good news more companies  are looking to turn recycled materials  into new products so we'll be putting a  list of the materials that you can  recycle in southern Nevada if you have  questions it's on our website  8newsnow.com for more information and  you know I talk to people all the time  about Recycling and they say well I'm  not really a good recycler I don't  really know what we're supposed to do  but Republic Services does a really good  job on their website and information on  top of your bin of what can go in and  what shouldn't go in and a lot of times  people just mix their garbage and then  that's all contaminated and it all has  to be thrown away so there's a lot of  controversy around recycling but there's  a lot of good success rates with our  recycling here too so please if you'd  like to recycle it goes a long way you  can it can help
 

